tree-sitter-cli (FULL_VERSION) DIST; urgency=low

  ## v0.27.0 (2026-08-30)

  CLI highlights (see the upstream release for the complete list):

  - `tree-sitter build` gains a `--verbose` flag, canonicalizes the `--output`
    path, supports concurrent builds of the same grammar in different
    locations, and warns when `nm` cannot verify the parser's symbols.
  - `tree-sitter test --update` rewrites all corpus files, and the test
    summary output is restored.
  - `tree-sitter init -u` reports what it updates and fixes several update
    issues; the `Package.swift` scanner detection works when the grammar is
    used as a dependency.
  - `tree-sitter generate` no longer requires `tree-sitter.json` for ABI 15,
    errors when a supertype is defined as a terminal, and is faster.
  - CST output fixes: trailing whitespace after multiline text nodes and
    `--no-ranges` discrepancies.
  - `tree-sitter highlight` sets the language in the current directory for
    every usage, and gains UTF-16 support.
  - Wasm: updated wasi-sdk and binaryen, cached toolchains are invalidated on
    version mismatch, several `realloc` fixes and stdlib additions.
  - Query fixes for captures in alternations with quantifiers.
  - Rust edition 2024, MSRV 1.90.

  Packaging note: the binary is compiled from the upstream v0.27.0 source tag
  on Ubuntu 22.04 (glibc 2.35), because upstream's prebuilt Linux binaries
  require glibc 2.39 and do not run on Debian 12 or Ubuntu 22.04.

  The complete upstream release notes live at
  https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter/releases/tag/v0.27.0
